      "## Gap six: the shop does not remember",
      "The customer has bought the same blood-pressure strip on the first of every month for six years. The app knows. The register does not. A refill reminder is the cheapest order a pharmacy will ever win, and almost none send one.",
      "## Gap seven: the shop is not on the phone",
      "This is the gap that contains the other six. The customer's day happens on a phone. The shop happens on a street. Everything the app does well, it does because it is in the pocket when the need arrives.",
      "> The customer did not leave because the app was cheaper. The customer left because the app answered.",
      "## None of this needs the chemist to build an app",
